<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Directs a large charitable foundation that serves low-income families; long working days, frequent public speaking, and travel. Wants to keep working as much as she can [S]</item><item>Married; no children. She asks that all news about her health be given to her first, and she alone decides what her family and her colleagues are told [S]</item><item>Language: Spanish is her preferred language for health care; she reads English but wants medical discussions in Spanish. Dr. Barragán speaks Spanish; a professional medical interpreter is booked for clinicians who do not. She declines family members as interpreters [S]</item><item>Screening: never had cervical screening; did not receive the HPV vaccine [S]</item><item>Tobacco: never smoked. Alcohol: a glass of wine on social occasions; no drugs [S]</item><item>Sexual and reproductive health: one male partner, her spouse; no pregnancies; no contraception at present [S]</item><item>Supports: a close friend and a long-time colleague at the foundation; her work gives her purpose. She would like the hospital&apos;s spiritual care team offered when she is in treatment [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

